<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Can you be obedient</l><l>To the Lord you serve,</l><l>Never even flinch, friend,</l><l>Never even swerve;</l><l>Though your next step onward</l><l>Seem to lead to death?</l><l>Can you then obey Him</l><l>Without bated breath?</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Can you trust your Leader</l><l>When He bids you go</l><l>Right into a battle</l><l>With a mighty foe?</l><l>Can you step up briskly</l><l>And with joy obey?</l><l>Can you fight the battle,</l><l>Till the end of day?</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Can you? Then beloved,</l><l>Christ just waits for you;</l><l>Listen for His orders,</l><l>Glad His will to do;</l><l>Then when soldiers muster</l><l>At the set of sun,</l><l>And your name is mentioned,</l><l>Christ will say, “Well done.”</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
